---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
---
<Docs slug="getting-started">
  <h1>Getting started</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Ouijit runs your coding agents side by side. Give each one a task, and it works in its own copy of the repo
    while you watch, review and merge.
  </p>

  <h2>Requirements</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>macOS</strong> 13 or later (Apple Silicon or Intel), or <strong>Linux</strong> x64</li>
    <li><strong>Git</strong> 2.20 or later</li>
    <li>An agent CLI: <code>claude</code>, <code>codex</code>, <code>pi</code> or <code>opencode</code></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <div class="docs-tabs">
    <div class="docs-tablist" role="tablist" aria-label="Platform">
      <button type="button" role="tab" id="install-tab-macos" aria-controls="install-macos" aria-selected="true">macOS</button>
      <button type="button" role="tab" id="install-tab-linux" aria-controls="install-linux" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Linux</button>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-tabpanel" role="tabpanel" id="install-macos" aria-labelledby="install-tab-macos" data-label="macOS">
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/ouijit/ouijit/releases/latest/download/ouijit-darwin-arm64.dmg">Apple Silicon</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/ouijit/ouijit/releases/latest/download/ouijit-darwin-x64.dmg">Intel</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Open the DMG and drag <strong>Ouijit.app</strong> into Applications.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-tabpanel" role="tabpanel" id="install-linux" aria-labelledby="install-tab-linux" data-label="Linux" hidden>
      <p>On Debian or Ubuntu, install the package:</p>
      <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>curl -LO https://github.com/ouijit/ouijit/releases/latest/download/ouijit-linux-x64.deb
sudo apt install ./ouijit-linux-x64.deb</code></pre>
      <p>Anywhere else, unzip the app into a folder and run it from there:</p>
      <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>curl -LO https://github.com/ouijit/ouijit/releases/latest/download/ouijit-linux-x64.zip
unzip ouijit-linux-x64.zip -d ~/.local/share
~/.local/share/ouijit-linux-x64/ouijit</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>Open Ouijit and add a project. Its board walks you through a practice task.</p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/docs/worktrees/">Worktrees</a>: how each task gets its own copy of the repo.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/hooks/">Hooks</a>: start your agent when a task starts.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/terminals/">Terminals</a>: the sidebar, the terminal stack and shortcuts.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/palette/">Command palette</a>: jump to anything with <code>⌘K</code>.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/panels/">Panels</a>: open the agent's plan, a dev server or a script beside its terminal.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/sandbox/">Sandbox</a>: let an agent run without permission prompts, kept to its worktree.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/pull-requests/">Pull requests</a>: review and merge in Ouijit.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Coming from another tool</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/conductor-alternative/">From Conductor</a> and <a href="/vibe-kanban-alternative/">from Vibe Kanban</a>
    map their ideas onto Ouijit's.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <p>
    Ouijit checks for updates when it opens and every hour after. On macOS it downloads the update and offers to
    restart; on Linux it links to the release. You can turn this off under
    <strong>App Settings &rarr; Updates</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>Missing tools</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Help &amp; setup</strong> lists the tools Ouijit looks for (git, the agent CLIs, <code>gh</code> and
    <code>nono</code>) and which ones it found. A feature that needs a missing tool says so where you use it.
  </p>

  <h2>Projects folder</h2>
  <p>
    Projects you create or clone go in <code>~/Ouijit/projects</code>. Change it under
    <strong>App Settings &rarr; Projects</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>Build from source</h2>
  <p>You need Node.js 20 or later and a C/C++ toolchain:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>macOS:</strong> <code>xcode-select --install</code></li>
    <li><strong>Linux:</strong> <code>sudo apt install build-essential python3</code> on Debian or Ubuntu</li>
  </ul>
  <pre class="glass-bevel"><code>git clone https://github.com/ouijit/ouijit.git
cd ouijit
npm install
npm start</code></pre>

  <h2>For agents</h2>
  <p>
    If you're an agent in an Ouijit terminal, <code>ouijit</code> is on your <code>PATH</code> and its reference
    is in your system prompt. Start with <a href="/docs/agents/">For agents</a>. Every page here is also plain
    Markdown at <code>/docs/&lt;slug&gt;.md</code>.
  </p>
</Docs>

<script>
  for (const tabs of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.docs-tabs')) {
    const buttons = [...tabs.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[role="tab"]')];
    const select = (chosen: HTMLButtonElement) => {
      for (const button of buttons) {
        const selected = button === chosen;
        button.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(selected));
        button.tabIndex = selected ? 0 : -1;
        document.getElementById(button.getAttribute('aria-controls') ?? '')!.hidden = !selected;
      }
    };
    buttons.forEach((button, i) => {
      button.addEventListener('click', () => select(button));
      button.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
        const step = e.key === 'ArrowRight' ? 1 : e.key === 'ArrowLeft' ? -1 : 0;
        if (!step) return;
        const next = buttons[(i + step + buttons.length) % buttons.length];
        select(next);
        next.focus();
      });
    });
    if (navigator.userAgent.includes('Linux')) select(buttons.find((b) => b.textContent === 'Linux') ?? buttons[0]);
  }

  // The docs lived on this one page before they were split up, so links like
  // /docs/#cli are still out in the wild. Forward them to the page that
  // section became.
  const LEGACY_SECTIONS: Record<string, string> = {
    worktrees: 'worktrees',
    kanban: 'worktrees',
    terminals: 'terminals',
    panels: 'panels',
    palette: 'palette',
    diff: 'diff',
    github: 'pull-requests',
    sandbox: 'sandbox',
    resume: 'terminals',
    themes: 'themes',
    hooks: 'hooks',
    harnesses: 'harnesses',
    agents: 'agents',
    cli: 'cli',
  };
  const target = LEGACY_SECTIONS[location.hash.replace('#', '')];
  if (target) location.replace(`/docs/${target}/`);
</script>
